+THE 100 Mb/s EGRESS ([PR #1020's ruling](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/1020#issuecomment-7216971645), #1004's merge gate) holds FR_NFR 3.4.1's `T_egress` at the Arty's 100BASE-TX, where the rings' capacity argument does not hold.
+- **The queue.** At a point whose shape states `phy: mii-100`, [`egress_queue.hpp`](egress_queue.hpp) decides the mailbox's `tx_ready` each cycle, so the census drains at link rate through the shipping transmit queue. In order: the control lane's byte crossing, 17 bytes; KL_ctrl_split's packer, eight bytes in nine datapath cycles; the 512-cycle minimum-gap gasket; the merges with the shape's SR frames (90 bytes each 125 us) and its gPTP frames (a burst of seven each 125 ms), a frame at a time; MilanMAC's store-and-forward FIFO, 512 words and 8 frames, each held to its last octet; and 80 ns a wire octet with preamble, padding, FCS and gap. The testbench prints the queue (`EGRESSQ`) and each control frame's last beat in and last octet out (`EGRESS`). A gigabit point states no queue, and its testbench and logs are unchanged.
+- **Why the census, not a replay.** Replayed through the queue, the instant-egress census changes the free-space test's outcome in 11 of its 159 cases (the ruling's item 2(a)). The firmware also reads TX_TAIL for AECP's completions and REBOOT's drain, besides the free-space test. Drained at link rate, every one of those reads is the firmware's own.
+- **The grade.** [`egress_mii.py`](egress_mii.py) `BUILD...` reads each queue parameter from its source (`milan_soc.py`, `milan_datapath.sv`, `mbx_contract.h` and the shape's configuration). It refuses a log whose queue differs and replays each case's commits through the same model in Python. Each record anchored to its last mailbox byte, that replay must reproduce every departure the testbench printed exactly, the beat in and the last octet; unanchored, from the commits alone, it sweeps the SR stream over eight phases. The row is the largest commit-to-last-octet wait of a record no hold meets, plus one whole gPTP burst, times 1.05, plus the fixed path, at most 1 ms. Held egress, and everything queued behind it, stays [`egress_ledger.py`](egress_ledger.py)'s.
+- **The fixed path**, 320 ns, is the converted MII chain's own (`tb/verilator/gptp_txts/generated/mac_tx_chain_mii.v`): [`egress_fixed.py`](egress_fixed.py) `BUILD_DIR` sends one frame at a time through it at the Arty's 80/50/25 MHz over 64 clock phases, and fails unless the stated figure is its largest, rounded up to 10 ns.
+- `egress_mii.py --selftest` runs eight controls and plants nine defects, each caught by its own control: a wire twice as fast, no gasket, a nine-frame FIFO, no SR stream, a grade drifted from its testbench, held egress counted, no margin, no gPTP burst, and an agreement loose enough to pass a departure one datapath cycle off. `--structural` prints AECP's admission burst (16 recipients at 1,514 bytes: 391.5 us each, 2.18 ms in all) and the rings at capacity (254 least records: 2.65 ms).
+- **At the Arty**, over the 159-case link-rate census, every departure agrees, the largest wait is 426.47 us (`answering-ports/aecp-largest-notice`, a 550-byte notice frame) and the row is 505.74 us. At most 19 records queue at once, and `backlog-owed` and `aecp-outputs` leave 26 and 18 held records to the ledger. The census derives the installed row again, a fixed point, and its qualification passes with this row checked as `egress-100`.
+
 [`load_grade.py`](load_grade.py) is the long-window load of every source at its stated arrival bound (#665, the round 24 ruling, item 2): each source's rate, a contract rate or a protocol timer, its clause in the module's term list and its value read from the tree, times its stated cost, at 1x1/1if, 8x8/2if and 32x32/2if.
 Its stated costs are `poll_grade.STATED_US`'s for the polls and `ctrl_loop.h`'s for THE TRANSMIT's builds and THE STEP at the two harness points, and its own `STATED_US` for the records, the events and a centisecond's consumers there and for every cost at 32x32/2if, measured on the 32x32 simulation shape (#859).
 That is the column at this tree's TSN stack pin. A second, `STATED_US_DONOR`, is measured with tsn-c-stack #32 applied at the pin in a scratch build (the ACMP core walking only the sinks an entry changed), each cost stated at every point. The gate holds 1x1/1if in both columns, the pin's being the image that merges and the donor's the load the pin move owes (#665), each named in what it finds (`load_grade.COLUMNS`), and reports both.

